<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - BP upped to buy.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - BP upped to buy.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- First Albany said analyst Mike Smolinski raised British Petroleum Plc to a buy from an underperform rating.</p>
<p>-- said end-of-winter drop in oil prices appears to be over.</p>
<p>-- estimates 1997 earnings $9.85 a share, compared with $8.74 in 1996.</p>
<p>-- estimates 1998 earnings $11.53 a share.</p>
<p>-- said stock price target is $162.</p>
<p>-- said colder temperatures are consuming inventory.</p>
<p>-- said believes world oil demand growing faster than consensus perceives.</p>
<p>-- said company is targeting $300 million in preformance improvement from lower costs and increased volumes for 1997.</p>
<p>-- British Petroleum stock was down 2-1/8 to 133-3/8 in morning trade.</p>
</text>
